2026-08-16T14:17:50Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE guidance: 3.48473 is 5.6% away from the guided midpoint 3.3 with no explicit range to justify it
2026-08-16T14:17:50Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Your value $3.48473 is above management’s stated FY2026 Q3 adjusted EPS guidance range of $3.30 ± $0.15 (i.e., $3.15–$3.45). It exceeds the top end by $0.0347 (~1%), so it contradicts the provided guidance for the exact metric and period.
2026-08-16T14:17:52Z    [DE:Worldwide net sales and revenues] GATE critic: The FY2024Q3→FY2025Q3 change you fed into the weighting is -8.6%, but Deere explicitly reported that worldwide net sales and revenues fell 9% to $12.018 billion in FY2025Q3. Using -8.6% instead of the reported -9.0% understates the decline and inflates your weighted YoY (-11.68%) and the FY2026Q3 estimate; correcting to -9% would push the implied YoY to ~-11.8% and the forecast down to roughly $10,602m, not $10,614.8m.
2026-08-16T14:18:16Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: The 72.4% is anchored to an average of (69.9, 71.6, 74.1, 72.2) drawn from FY2020Q3–FY2023Q3, and even includes 69.9% which appears to be a prior‑year comparator on those lines rather than the reported Q3 margin; this omits the most recent Q3s (e.g., FY2024Q3, FY2025Q3) and misidentifies periods, so the baseline is stale and on the wrong period basis for FY2026Q3.
